{"t": 51.645, "n": 41, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the triage note to `plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i170c.triage.md`. I didn't run the repository's triage check. The note lists seven gaps and routes the run to discovery.\n\nI opened `task-notes.rule.md` and `documents.rule.md`, both under `.claude/rules/temperspec/`, with the read tool. I also read `runs-without-a-final-exit.spec.md` and the SIL-B2/B3/B19 section of `self-improvement.spec.md`. For `loop-issues.spec.md`, `engine-cli.spec.md` and the guide I read only grep matches. I checked the engine code by search only, not by reading the files.\n\n- **Criteria:** the task numbers its criteria 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 and skips 5. I kept those numbers as written.\n- **Gaps:** G1 to G6 are findable spec updates, spec gaps or an existing behaviour:\n  - G1 is the delivery checks and age limit for the outbox.\n  - G2 is the outbox list and clear verbs.\n  - G3 is the re-handing of pause findings.\n  - G4 is the operator reason.\n  - G5 is that the pattern count takes only `fault` lines.\n  - G6 is how a finding line with no `segment_started` is bound to its segment.\n- **Covered gap:** G7 (the pause's own reason in an issue body) ends `Covered by ISS-B14 and ISS-AC13`, because the code disagrees with a spec that is already right. It is the only covered gap, so not every gap is covered and discovery takes the full visit.\n- **Owner decisions:** `None`. Every gap can be answered from the code or the documents.\n\nARTIFACT triage_note: plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i170c.triage.md\nARTIFACT gaps: some\nARTIFACT route: discovery\nARTIFACT covered: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "9382d6f9-410a-4251-a107-1c6ec9b35734"}
